It is eight o'clock.
The game is over and we are all tired.
We cannot run anymore.
We pack our things.
I put my water bottle into the backpack.
Lena looks at me.
"Do you want to come back next Thursday?", she asks.
"We always play at half past five," says Max.
I definitely want to come back.
"Yes, very gladly!", I answer.
"I can be here on Thursday at half past five."
Timo laughs and takes his bag.
"Super, see you next week then!", he says.
We say goodbye.
The others go outside.
I go to the reception desk.
I give the racket back to the staff member.
"Here is the racket, thank you very much," I say.
"Are you playing again next week?", he asks.
"Yes, I want to play every Thursday now," I answer.
